      {
        "id": 64918,
        "name": "Ironic",
        "username": "Ironic",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-06-13T18:06:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Sentinels really has more of a Bronze Age/Modern Age thing going on, though - and during those periods, ape villains have been pretty well put on the backburner. &nbsp;If Sentinels were a \"Silver Age game,\" the environment decks would full of things like \"Romantic Interest Marring a Robot\" and \"You're Really Ugly - The Public Turns Against You,\" while the villains would all be playing cards based on practical jokes or absurd deceptions which amount to nothing, instead of killing people in cold blood.</p><p>Actually, though, that environment sounds pretty great. &nbsp;Maybe this isn't such a bad idea...</p><p>Ironic</p>",
