      {
        "id": 64920,
        "name": "Ironic",
        "username": "Ironic",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-06-13T18:24:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There's comedic beats lots of places, sure. &nbsp;But in surprise shopping trip, the joke is that the fight between the posthuman serial killer and the woman slowly being destroyed by dark magics has (due to a temporal anomaly) spilled over into a mundane setting. &nbsp;It's not like Legacy and Baron Blade have netered a pie-eating contest to design the sign for the new Megalopolis Mall (Blade wants to hide a death ray in the sign or something, Paul will give the contract to a silversmith friend who will otherwise go out of business) - that's a whole different level of crazy, one which we only really see in the form of Wraith's Action Hairdrier.</p><p>Ironic</p>",
